.PP
.PP
  
.SS "fastqueue([that], worker, concurrency)"
Creates a new queue\&.

.PP
Arguments:

.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRthat\fP, optional context of the \fRworker\fP function\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRworker\fP, worker function, it would be called with \fRthat\fP as \fRthis\fP, if that is specified\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRconcurrency\fP, number of concurrent tasks that could be executed in parallel\&.
.PP

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.push(task, done)"
Add a task at the end of the queue\&. \fRdone(err, result)\fP will be called when the task was processed\&.

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.unshift(task, done)"
Add a task at the beginning of the queue\&. \fRdone(err, result)\fP will be called when the task was processed\&.

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.pause()"
Pause the processing of tasks\&. Currently worked tasks are not stopped\&.

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.resume()"
Resume the processing of tasks\&.

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.idle()"
Returns \fRfalse\fP if there are tasks being processed or waiting to be processed\&. \fRtrue\fP otherwise\&.

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.length()"
Returns the number of tasks waiting to be processed (in the queue)\&.

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.getQueue()"
Returns all the tasks be processed (in the queue)\&. Returns empty array when there are no tasks

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.kill()"
Removes all tasks waiting to be processed, and reset \fRdrain\fP to an empty function\&.

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.killAndDrain()"
Same than \fRkill\fP but the \fRdrain\fP function will be called before reset to empty\&.

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.error(handler)"
Set a global error handler\&. \fRhandler(err, task)\fP will be called each time a task is completed, \fRerr\fP will be not null if the task has thrown an error\&.

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.concurrency"
Property that returns the number of concurrent tasks that could be executed in parallel\&. It can be altered at runtime\&.

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.paused"
Property (Read-Only) that returns \fRtrue\fP when the queue is in a paused state\&.

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.drain"
Function that will be called when the last item from the queue has been processed by a worker\&. It can be altered at runtime\&.

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.empty"
Function that will be called when the last item from the queue has been assigned to a worker\&. It can be altered at runtime\&.

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "queue\&.saturated"
Function that will be called when the queue hits the concurrency limit\&. It can be altered at runtime\&.

.PP
.PP
  
.SS "fastqueue\&.promise([that], worker(arg), concurrency)"
Creates a new queue with \fRPromise\fP apis\&. It also offers all the methods and properties of the object returned by \fB`fastqueue`\fP with the modified \fB`push`\fP and \fB`unshift`\fP methods\&.

.PP
Node v10+ is required to use the promisified version\&.

.PP
Arguments:
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRthat\fP, optional context of the \fRworker\fP function\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRworker\fP, worker function, it would be called with \fRthat\fP as \fRthis\fP, if that is specified\&. It MUST return a \fRPromise\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRconcurrency\fP, number of concurrent tasks that could be executed in parallel\&.
.PP

.PP
 
.SS "queue\&.push(task) => Promise"
Add a task at the end of the queue\&. The returned \fRPromise\fP will be fulfilled (rejected) when the task is completed successfully (unsuccessfully)\&.

.PP
This promise could be ignored as it will not lead to a \fR'unhandledRejection'\fP\&.

.PP
 
.SS "queue\&.unshift(task) => Promise"
Add a task at the beginning of the queue\&. The returned \fRPromise\fP will be fulfilled (rejected) when the task is completed successfully (unsuccessfully)\&.

.PP
This promise could be ignored as it will not lead to a \fR'unhandledRejection'\fP\&.

.PP
 
.SS "queue\&.drained() => Promise"
Wait for the queue to be drained\&. The returned \fRPromise\fP will be resolved when all tasks in the queue have been processed by a worker\&.

.PP
This promise could be ignored as it will not lead to a \fR'unhandledRejection'\fP\&.
